KNN => K-  Nearest Neighbour

K => no of relationships

KNN is calculated based upon the proximity or closeness. This Proximity and closeness is decided by distanced based
Algorithm

Distance based metrics/formula:

1. Manhattan Distance
2. Euclidean Distance


KNN can be used for both classification and Regression

Note:
    => This is one of the Non-Parametric algorithm
    => It is widely applied for non linear data set

Parametric:
    It is nothing but getting the detail only by its column specific distributions

Non - Parametric:
    It never  assumes any specific forms of the data but it check overall data range


K value should always be odd number
k value depends on data set
Elbow method is used to find K values


